  <title>Common Problems</title>

  <section id="network">
    <title>Network</title>
    <p>
      If the computer has no network, Babble says so in a banner and keeps
      trying; the banner goes away by itself once the network is back.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="login">
    <title>Logins</title>
    <p>
      If a login disappears from the keyring, Babble forgets that account
      rather than retrying forever. Sign in again from the welcome screen.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="keyring">
    <title>Keyring</title>
    <p>
      Babble keeps every login in the system keyring, so it needs a keyring
      service such as GNOME Keyring or KeePassXC to be running. If none is,
      Babble says so when it starts or when you sign in, and keeps the
      account it already has. Start a keyring service and restart Babble.
      In a Flatpak, the app needs permission to talk to
      <code>org.freedesktop.secrets</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="server">
    <title>Server compatibility</title>
    <p>
      A server that does not support a feature hides it: Collections and the
      Admin Dashboard appear only where the server has them, so an older
      Mastodon shows a smaller menu rather than an error.
    </p>
  </section>

</page>